---
<Layout title="Privacy Policy | Luxury Modules" description="How Luxury Modules collects, uses and protects your personal data, the lawful basis for processing, and your rights under UK GDPR." noindex={false}>
<div class="pagehero">
  <p class="kicker">Legal</p>
  <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
  <p>How we handle your personal data, why we hold it, and the rights you have over it.</p>
  <p style="font-size:13px;color:var(--muted);margin-top:10px">Last updated: {updated}</p>
</div>

<section><div class="wrap" style="max-width:820px">

  <h2>Who we are</h2><div class="gold-rule"></div>
  <p>Luxury Modules Limited is the data controller for the personal data described in this notice. We are registered in England and Wales, company number 16007852, with our registered office at 111-113 High Street, Evesham, Worcestershire, WR11 4XP.</p>
  <p>For any question about this notice or about your personal data, contact us at <a href="mailto:sales@luxurymodules.co.uk">sales@luxurymodules.co.uk</a>.</p>

  <h2 style="margin-top:44px">What we collect and why</h2><div class="gold-rule"></div>
  <p>We collect only what we need to answer an enquiry and, where you ask us to, to design and quote for a project.</p>
  <p><b>When you request the brochure</b> we collect your first name and email address, so that we can send you the brochure and price list.</p>
  <p><b>When you book a scoping call</b> we collect your name, email address, phone number, the location of your land and any project detail you choose to give us, so that we can prepare for and hold that conversation.</p>
  <p><b>When you use the module configurator</b> we collect your name, email address, phone number, installation postcode, your chosen specification and any notes you add, so that we can confirm the specification and issue a reservation invoice if you ask us to.</p>
  <p><b>When you browse the site</b> and consent to statistics cookies, we collect analytics data about how the site is used. This is described in our <a href="/cookies/">Cookie Policy</a>.</p>

  <h2 style="margin-top:44px">Our lawful basis</h2><div class="gold-rule"></div>
  <p>For enquiries, scoping calls and configurator submissions we rely on <b>legitimate interests</b>: you have approached us about a project and we have a clear interest in responding. Where a project proceeds, we rely on <b>performance of a contract</b>.</p>
  <p>For analytics cookies and for marketing emails beyond the material you asked for, we rely on <b>consent</b>, which you give through the cookie banner or by opting in, and which you can withdraw at any time.</p>

  <h2 style="margin-top:44px">Who processes your data</h2><div class="gold-rule"></div>
  <p>We do not sell personal data and we do not share it for third-party advertising. We use the following processors, each of which handles data on our instructions:</p>
  <p><b>HubSpot</b> (HubSpot Ireland Limited) hosts our customer records and processes the three forms on this site. Data is held in HubSpot's EU infrastructure.</p>
  <p><b>Google Analytics 4</b> (Google Ireland Limited) provides aggregate statistics about site usage, where you have consented to statistics cookies.</p>
  <p><b>Microsoft Clarity</b> (Microsoft Ireland Operations Limited) provides aggregate usage and interaction analytics, where you have consented to statistics cookies.</p>
  <p><b>Cookiebot</b> (Usercentrics A/S) records your consent choices so that we can demonstrate compliance.</p>
  <p><b>Vercel</b> (Vercel Inc.) hosts this website and processes standard server request data.</p>
  <p>Some of these providers may transfer data outside the UK. Where they do, transfers are covered by UK International Data Transfer Agreements, the EU Standard Contractual Clauses with the UK Addendum, or an adequacy decision.</p>

  <h2 style="margin-top:44px">How long we keep it</h2><div class="gold-rule"></div>
  <p>Enquiry and brochure records are kept for up to three years from your last contact with us, after which they are deleted. Records relating to a project we have delivered are kept for seven years to meet accounting and warranty obligations. Analytics data is retained according to the settings in each platform, currently up to fourteen months.</p>

  <h2 style="margin-top:44px">Your rights</h2><div class="gold-rule"></div>
  <p>Under UK GDPR you have the right to ask us for a copy of your personal data, to have inaccurate data corrected, to have data erased, to restrict or object to processing, and to receive your data in a portable format. Where we rely on consent, you can withdraw it at any time without affecting processing that has already taken place.</p>
  <p>To exercise any of these rights, email <a href="mailto:sales@luxurymodules.co.uk">sales@luxurymodules.co.uk</a>. We will respond within one month.</p>
  <p>If you are unhappy with how we have handled your data you can complain to the Information Commissioner's Office, the UK supervisory authority, at <a href="https://ico.org.uk" rel="noopener">ico.org.uk</a> or on 0303 123 1113. We would appreciate the chance to put things right first.</p>

  <h2 style="margin-top:44px">Changes to this notice</h2><div class="gold-rule"></div>
  <p>We will update this page when our processing changes, and the date at the top will change with it.</p>

  <div style="margin-top:40px"><a class="btn" href="/cookies/">Cookie Policy</a> <a class="btn ghost" href="/terms/" style="margin-left:8px">Terms &amp; Conditions</a></div>
</div></section>
</Layout>
